# AxDiagnostics (system_ext priv-app, system_app domain) reads kernel
# performance counters to populate its CPU, memory, I/O and thermal pages.
# Stock policy grants appdomain only proc_meminfo, so these reads fail with
# EACCES and the affected pages have no data.
#
# These are read-only, system-wide performance counters. system_app is a
# platform-signed, in-ROM domain and is NOT part of the all_untrusted_apps
# neverallow set in system/sepolicy/private/app_neverallows.te, so granting
# read here is permitted by policy.
#
# Deliberately NOT granted: /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches and
# /proc/sys/vm/compact_memory, which are writable kernel controls rather than
# counters. The corresponding AxDiagnostics actions stay non-functional.
allow system_app proc_loadavg:file r_file_perms;
allow system_app proc_stat:file r_file_perms;
allow system_app proc_diskstats:file r_file_perms;
allow system_app proc_vmstat:file r_file_perms;
allow system_app proc_pressure_cpu:file r_file_perms;
allow system_app proc_pressure_io:file r_file_perms;
allow system_app proc_pressure_mem:file r_file_perms;
